<h3>Update User Profile</h3>

<p><code>PUT /users/{userId}/profile</code></p>

<p>
    Updates the user's shared first name, last name, and email
    across all applications managed by AppUser.
    Username, UserID, account status, roles, and application
    assignments remain unchanged.
</p>

<p>
    Requires Windows Authentication and an active registered caller.
    ModifiedBy is determined by the API from the authenticated identity.
    Clients do not supply audit fields.
</p>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Required</th>
            <th>Validation</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>firstName</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>Maximum 100 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>lastName</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>Maximum 100 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>email</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>
                Valid email format, maximum 255 characters,
                unique across users.
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    Supply all three fields. Values are trimmed before storage.
    Another user's email cannot be used, including an inactive user's email.
</p>

<h5>Example request</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "firstName": "Javier",
  "lastName": "DeJesus",
  "email": "domingo.dejesus@advantagelife.com"
&#125;</code></pre>

<h5>Example response — 200 OK</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 0,
  "userID": 1,
  "message": "User profile updated successfully."
&#125;</code></pre>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Return code</th>
            <th>HTTP status</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>200</td>
            <td>Profile updated.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>404</td>
            <td>Target user does not exist.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2–7</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>A required field is missing or exceeds its maximum length.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>8</td>
            <td>409</td>
            <td>Email already belongs to another user.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>9</td>
            <td>403</td>
            <td>Audit user does not exist or is inactive.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>10</td>
            <td>200</td>
            <td>Profile is unchanged; no update performed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>11</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Email format is invalid.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    Actual changes update ModifiedDate in UTC and ModifiedBy.
    Creation fields are preserved.
    Unchanged saves preserve modification fields as well.
</p>

<p>
    Unauthenticated requests receive HTTP 401.
    An authenticated caller who cannot be resolved to an active
    registered user receives HTTP 403.
    Unexpected server errors receive HTTP 500.
    Forbidden and unexpected-error responses use Problem Details.
</p>

<hr />

<h3>Application Management</h3>

<table class="table table-striped">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Method</th>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>GET</td>
            <td><code>/applications</code></td>
            <td>
                Lists applications, including their code, name,
                description, and active status.
                Includes inactive applications.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>GET</td>
            <td><code>/applications/{applicationId}/roles</code></td>
            <td>
                Lists the application's roles, descriptions,
                and active statuses. Includes inactive roles.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>POST</td>
            <td><code>/applications</code></td>
            <td>Creates an application.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>POST</td>
            <td><code>/applications/{applicationId}/roles</code></td>
            <td>Creates a role for an application.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>PUT</td>
            <td><code>/applications/{applicationId}/description</code></td>
            <td>Updates or clears an application's description.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>PUT</td>
            <td>
                <code>/applications/{applicationId}/roles/{roleId}/description</code>
            </td>
            <td>Updates or clears a role's description.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<div class="alert alert-info">
    All POST and PUT endpoints in this section require Windows
    Authentication and an active registered user.
    The API determines CreatedBy and ModifiedBy from that identity.
    Clients do not supply audit fields.
</div>

<h4>Create Application</h4>

<p><code>POST /applications</code></p>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Required</th>
            <th>Maximum length</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>applicationCode</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>25</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>applicationName</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>100</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>description</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>255</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    Application codes and names must each be unique,
    including against inactive applications.
    Values are trimmed; blank descriptions are stored as NULL.
    New applications start active.
    Roles and user assignments must be added separately.
</p>

<h5>Example request</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "applicationCode": "SAMPLE_APP",
  "applicationName": "Sample Application",
  "description": "Example application."
&#125;</code></pre>

<h5>Example response — 201 Created</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 0,
  "applicationID": 8,
  "message": "Application created successfully."
&#125;</code></pre>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Return code</th>
            <th>HTTP status</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>201</td>
            <td>Application created.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Application code is required.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Application code exceeds 25 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>3</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Application name is required.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>4</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Application name exceeds 100 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>5</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Description exceeds 255 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>6</td>
            <td>409</td>
            <td>Application code already exists.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>7</td>
            <td>409</td>
            <td>Application name already exists.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>8</td>
            <td>403</td>
            <td>Audit user does not exist or is inactive.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<hr />

<h4>Create Application Role</h4>

<p><code>POST /applications/{applicationId}/roles</code></p>

<p>
    Role name is required and limited to 50 characters.
    Description is optional and limited to 255 characters.
    Values are trimmed.
    The application must exist and be active.
    Role names must be unique within the application,
    including against inactive roles.
</p>

<h5>Example request</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "roleName": "Viewer",
  "description": "Read-only access."
&#125;</code></pre>

<h5>Example response — 201 Created</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 0,
  "roleID": 20,
  "applicationID": 8,
  "message": "Application role created successfully."
&#125;</code></pre>

<p>
    New roles start active. Creating a role does not assign users
    or implement permission checks in the consuming application.
</p>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Return code</th>
            <th>HTTP status</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>201</td>
            <td>Role created.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Application does not exist or is inactive.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Role name is required.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>3</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Role name exceeds 50 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>4</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Description exceeds 255 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>5</td>
            <td>409</td>
            <td>Role name already exists for this application.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>6</td>
            <td>403</td>
            <td>Audit user does not exist or is inactive.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<hr />

<h4>Update Application or Role Description</h4>

<p><code>PUT /applications/{applicationId}/description</code></p>

<p>
    <code>PUT /applications/{applicationId}/roles/{roleId}/description</code>
</p>

<p>
    Both endpoints accept the same request structure.
    Description is limited to 255 characters and is trimmed.
    An omitted, NULL, empty, or whitespace-only description clears it.
    Names, codes, active statuses, and user assignments remain unchanged.
</p>

<h5>Example request</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "description": "Updated description."
&#125;</code></pre>

<h5>Application response — 200 OK</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 0,
  "applicationID": 8,
  "message": "Application description updated successfully."
&#125;</code></pre>

<h5>Role response — 200 OK</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 0,
  "roleID": 20,
  "applicationID": 8,
  "message": "Role description updated successfully."
&#125;</code></pre>

<table class="table table-sm">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Return code</th>
            <th>HTTP status</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td>0</td>
            <td>200</td>
            <td>Description updated.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>404</td>
            <td>
                Application not found, or role not found
                within the specified application.
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>2</td>
            <td>400</td>
            <td>Description exceeds 255 characters.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>3</td>
            <td>403</td>
            <td>Audit user does not exist or is inactive.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>4</td>
            <td>200</td>
            <td>Description is unchanged; no update performed.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p>
    An actual change updates ModifiedDate in UTC and records the
    authenticated user's ID in ModifiedBy. Creation fields are preserved.
    Saving an unchanged description preserves the modification fields too.
</p>

<hr />

<h4>Application Management Error Responses</h4>

<p>
    Unauthenticated write requests receive HTTP 401.
    An authenticated identity that cannot be resolved to an active
    registered user receives HTTP 403.
    Unexpected server errors receive HTTP 500.
</p>

<p>
    Validation and duplicate errors use returnCode and message.
    Forbidden and unexpected-error responses use Problem Details
    with a detail field. Clients should handle both response formats.
    IDs in the examples above are illustrative.
</p>

<h5>Example duplicate application response — 409 Conflict</h5>

<pre class="bg-light border rounded p-3"><code>&#123;
  "returnCode": 6,
  "applicationID": null,
  "message": "Application code already exists."
&#125;</code></pre>

<hr />

<h3>Authentication and Audit Behavior</h3>

<div class="alert alert-info">
    <p>
        <strong>Authentication:</strong>
        Protected API endpoints currently use Windows Authentication.
    </p>

<p>
    <strong>Application authorization:</strong>
    Being authenticated does not automatically grant access to an application.
    Application assignments and roles are maintained in the
    <code>Security</code> schema.
</p>

<p class="mb-0">
    <strong>Audit identity:</strong>
    <code>CreatedBy</code> and <code>ModifiedBy</code> are determined by the API
    from the authenticated user. Clients do not supply these values.
</p>

</div>

<hr />

<h3>Current API Base Address</h3>

<p>
    <code>https://localhost:7098</code>
</p>

<p class="text-muted">
    This address reflects the current local development environment and may change
    when the application is hosted.
</p>

@code {
    private List<ApplicationLookup>? applications;
    private List<RoleLookup>? roles;
    private List<SecurityUser>? users;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        applications = await ApplicationUserService.GetApplicationsAsync();

        roles = await ApplicationUserService.GetApplicationRolesAsync(3);

        users = await ApplicationUserService.GetUsersAsync();
    }
}